# SQL's `count(*)`: DS0117 with a fix to `count()`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | summarize n = count(*) by customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..52
  PIPELINE@0..51
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    SUMMARIZE_OP@15..51
      IDENT@15..24 "summarize"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@25..37
        NAME@25..26
          IDENT@25..26 "n"
        WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
        EQ@27..28 "="
        WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
        CALL_EXPR@29..37
          NAME_REF@29..34
            IDENT@29..34 "count"
          ARG_LIST@34..37
            L_PAREN@34..35 "("
            ERROR@35..36
              STAR@35..36 "*"
            R_PAREN@36..37 ")"
      WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
      BY_CLAUSE@38..51
        IDENT@38..40 "by"
        WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
        NAMED_EXPR@41..51
          NAME_REF@41..51
            IDENT@41..51 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@51..52 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `count(*)` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:36
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | summarize n = count(*) by customerId
  |                                    ^ `count()` counts rows without a `*`
  |
  = help: write `count()`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | summarize n = count() by customerId
which parses without errors
